Documentation for ppg
---------------------
rev 0.1, 2/2/99

The ppg generator is used to derive simple partial product generation logic
for a multiplier.

GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NBITS_A:
    Definition:
      The number of bits in input value A_H.  The number of partial 
      products generated will be NBITS_A + NBITS_B.  The width of each
      partial product will be max(NBITS_A, NBITS_B).
    Legal Values:
      1 <= n <= 63
    Default:
      8

  NBITS_B:
    Definition:
      The number of bits in input value B_H.  The number of partial 
      products generated will be NBITS_A + NBITS_B.  The width of each
      partial product will be max(NBITS_A, NBITS_B).
    Legal Values:
      1 <= n <= 63
    Default:
      8

  SignExtendInputs:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify whether the ppg logic's
      inputs are sign or zero extended.
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" (perform sign extension) 
      and "N" (perform zero extension).
    Default:
      N

  Algorithm:
    Definition:
      This argument allows the user to specify the partial product
      generation algorithm.
    Legal Values:
      Simple
    Default:
      Simple

  bitslice:    
    Definition:
      This argument directs DPC to enforce bitslice layout, or not.  
    Legal Values:
      The allowed values of this argument are "Y" and "N".
    Default:
      Y


INPUT SIGNALS:
--------------
  A_H (multiplier) and B_H (multiplicand)


OUTPUT SIGNALS:
---------------
  PP*_H (partial product vectors)


